      "id": "opening",
      "sceneId": "opening",
      "text": "The Library of Alexandria became a lasting symbol of humanity's ambition to gather knowledge.",
      "startFrame": 15,
      "endFrame": 141
    },
    {
      "id": "city",
      "sceneId": "city",
      "text": "In Ptolemaic Egypt, Alexandria grew into a center where scholars studied texts from across the Mediterranean world.",
      "startFrame": 186,
      "endFrame": 366
    },
    {
      "id": "timeline",
      "sceneId": "timeline",
      "text": "The institution was not created, transformed, or lost in a single dramatic moment.",
      "startFrame": 411,
      "endFrame": 546
    },
    {
      "id": "myth",
      "sceneId": "myth",
      "text": "Modern historians usually treat the library's decline as a complex process rather than one total destruction event.",
      "startFrame": 591,
      "endFrame": 756
    },
    {
      "id": "legacy",
      "sceneId": "legacy",
      "text": "Whatever its exact size and fate, Alexandria still represents the hope that collected knowledge can outlast any one generation.",
      "startFrame": 801,
      "endFrame": 981
    }
  ],
